sequenceDiagram

  actor C as Client
  participant G as Route guard<br/>composed middleware<br/>ENFORCEMENT POINT 1
  participant H as Route handler
  participant S as RequestService<br/>ENFORCEMENT POINT 2
  participant DB as MongoDB Atlas<br/>DEC-002
  participant Z as Response serialiser<br/>ENFORCEMENT POINT 3
  participant R as Authorisation rule set<br/>single documented source

  Note over G,R: All three enforcement points evaluate the same rule set.<br/>The rule set is single — the enforcement is distributed — DEC-012.

  alt Path A — refused at the route boundary (function-level access, FR-1.3 / FR-6.4)
    C->>G: PUT /requests/:id/status
    G->>R: may this role perform this operation?
    R-->>G: no
    G-->>C: 403 Forbidden
    Note over H,DB: The handler, the service and the database are never reached.<br/>A route registered without its guard is the failure mode —<br/>an automated assertion over the route table is the NFR-3.3 evidence.

  else Path B — permitted at the boundary, refused in the service (object-level access, FR-3.6 / FR-4.1)
    C->>G: GET /requests/:id
    G->>R: may this role perform this operation?
    R-->>G: yes
    G->>H: next()
    H->>S: getRequest(id, actor)
    S->>DB: findOne({ _id: id })
    DB-->>S: request document
    S->>R: may this actor see THIS request?
    R-->>S: no — not the owner, not the assigned department
    S-->>H: AuthorisationError
    H-->>C: 403 Forbidden
    Note over G,S: The boundary could not have made this decision.<br/>The rule depends on the document, and the document<br/>is not loaded until after the middleware chain has run.

  else Path C — permitted at both points, restricted at the serialiser (field-level access, FR-1.5 / FR-3.5 / NFR-4.4)
    C->>G: GET /requests/:id
    G->>R: may this role perform this operation?
    R-->>G: yes
    G->>H: next()
    H->>S: getRequest(id, actor)
    S->>DB: findOne({ _id: id })
    DB-->>S: request document<br/>security category — CFL-002
    S->>R: may this actor see THIS request?
    R-->>S: yes
    S-->>H: request document
    H->>Z: serialise(document, actor)
    Z->>R: which fields may this actor see?
    R-->>Z: reporter identity withheld
    Z-->>C: 200 OK — restricted projection
    Note over S,R: The record is visible — the restricted fields are not.<br/>This rule rests on the CFL-002 resolution, which is still<br/>Proposed — condition C-01 is open, exposure tracked as RSK-009.
  end
